[
  {
    "id": "c001",
    "name": "1.01. Initial Term",
    "text": "1. !!ill! 1.01. The Term of this agreement will begin on the date hereof and continue, unless extended as provided herein, for a first Contract Period (sometimes referred to as the -Initial Period·) ending eight (S) months after delivery of the Master Recordings comprising the Recording Obligation for such Period."
  },
  {
    "id": "c002",
    "name": "1.02. Extension Options",
    "text": "1. 02. Grantor grants PRI three (3) separate options to extend the Term for additional Contract Periods (sometimes referred to as \"Option Periods·). par may exercise each of those options by sending G:antor a notice at any time before the expiration of the Contract Period then in effect. If PRI exercises such an option, the Option Period concerned will commence upon the end of the current Contract Period (or, if PRr so advises, such period will begin on the date of such exercise notice) and end eight (8) months after delivery of the last Master Recordings comprising the Recording Obligation for such Contract Period."
  },
  {
    "id": "c003",
    "name": "2.01. Exclusive Recording Services",
    "text": "2. RECORD!NG OBLIGATION 2.01. PRr hereby engages Grantor to furnish the exclusive services of ~NGWIE MALMSTEEN (the -Artist-) and the services of individual produeers to produce and deliver to PRI Master Recordings as provided for herein. Grantor warrants that during the Term Artist shall perform for the purpose of making Phonograph Records exclusivel~ for Grantor and P~I."
  },
  {
    "id": "c004",
    "name": "2.02. Minimum Recording Obligation",
    "text": "2.02. During each Contract Period, Artist will perform for and Grantor will record and deliver a minimu·n number of Master Recordings (-Minimum Recording Obligation-) specified in the [allowing SChedule: Contract Period r.,inilr.um Reccrding Obligati~n Initial Two (2) Albums First Option Two (2) Albums Second Option Two (2) Albums Third Option Two (2) Albums"
  },
  {
    "id": "c005",
    "name": "3.01. Recording Services Standards",
    "text": "3. PROCEDURES 3.01. Grantor shall be responsible for coordination of recording sessions and Grantor, Artist and the individual producers shall render their services subject to the terms and conditions hereof to the best of their ability and in accordance with first-class standards for production in the Phonoaraph Record industry."
  },
  {
    "id": "c006",
    "name": "3.02. Recording Approvals and Procedures",
    "text": "3.02. Prior to Making each Recording, Grantor shall obtain PRI's approval, of each of the following in order, before proceeding fUrther: (t) selection of the individual producer of the Master Recordings hereunder, provided, however, that Artist is hereby deemed approved as the co-producer of all Master RecQrdings hereunder, it being understood and agreed that PRl and Grantor shall mutually agree upon the selection of the other co-producer, it being understood and agreed further, however, that Grantor shall have the sole tight to select the co-producer of any Album of the Minimum Recording Obligation to be recorded hereunder if Net Sales in the United States of the immediately preceding Album of the Minimum Recording Obligation hereunder exceed three hundred fifty thousand (350,000) units as of the end of the accounting period i~mediately prior to the commencement of recording of the Album in question, (ii) selection of Compositions to be recorded; PRI lIIay disapprove any Composition only if it might constitute a defama:ion, libel or violate or infringe upon any right, including, without limitation, the right of privacy, of any Person whatsoever, or which is subject to Objection for any other legal reason whatsoever in the reasonable opinion of PRI's counsel, and (iii) selection of studios where recording is to take place: PRl may disapprove a studio if its U3e would be inconsistent with any of PRIes union agreements, or if PRI anticipates that its use would cause labor difficulties for other reasons, or would require expenditures in excess of the approved recording budget, or would otherwise in any way substantially hinder or prevent the recordin9, manufacture or release of the applicable Master Recordings. At least fourteen (14) days pr ior to the date of the first recording session for the recording of any Master Recordings, the Grantor will subnit to PRI f~r its written approval, a written proposed budget setting forth, in itemized detail, all antiCipated Recording Costs. Without limitation of the foregoing obligation to submit a budget and/or of PRltS right of approval with respect to the specifics theito, with respect to th~ first Album of the MinimUM Recording Obligation, an aggregate budget amoant equal to the applicable Advance payable therefor pursuant to paragraph 6.0Hb) below is hereby deel:led approved and, with respect to each Album of the Minimum Recording Obligation hereunder after 0774/5080A/07B4A/5271A PSS-156 . CONFIDENTIAL UMG-MAL 001339 • - 3 - the first Album, an aggregate budget amount equal to the lesser of the amount of the applicable Advance payable pursuant to paragraph 6.0l(b) with respect to a particular Album of the Minimum Recording Obligation, or the amount equal to one hundred twenty percent (120%) of the Recording Costs for t!le immediately preceding Album is hereby deemed approved with respect to the particular Album. The sCheduling and bOOking of all studio time will be done by PRl, provided, however, that PRl shall authorize Grantor to do such scheduling and booking if, in advance of any studio time use, Grantor fUrnishes PRI with a letter from the applicable studio confirming that said studio will look only to Grantor and not to PRl for payment for any studio time scheduled and booked by Grantor. Grantor shall notify the appropriate local of the American Federation of Musicians in advance of each recording session. Grantor shall allow PRI representatives to attend any or all recording sessions hereunder upon reasonable notice to Grantor."
  },
  {
    "id": "c007",
    "name": "3.03. Delivery of Masters and Work Parts",
    "text": "3.03. With respect to Master Recordings hereunder, Grantor shall deliver to PRl equalized tape masters and reference discs which are representative of such tape masters, which reference discs and tapes shall be technically satisfactory for the manufacture and sale of Phonograph Records hereunder and shall embody Recordings that are -first-class- (as that term is understood in the record industry). Upon PRI's request, Grantor shall re-record any Composition until a technically satisfactory Master Recording shall have been obtained. Grantor shall edit, sequence, and leader multi-track master tapes for Master Recordings hereunder, in parallel sequence to any tWo-track m~ster tapes delivered hereunder, and shall further deliver same to PRl. With respect to each Master Recording delivered by Grantor hereunder, all work parts of whatever nature (including, without limitation, out-takes or other tracks recorded during the Term) shall be deli vered to PRI concurrently with delivery of the foregoing items under this paragraph 3.03, it being understood that PRI's use of such out-takes shall be subject to the terms of paragraph S.Ol(b)(i)."
  },
  {
    "id": "c008",
    "name": "3.04. Recording Information and Clearances",
    "text": "3.04. Grantor shall furnish PRl in writing with all information, consents and clearances required for the I manufacture and distribution of Phonograph Records hereunder including, without limitation, the label copy (including song titles and any subtitles), names of composers, complete publisher line, music performing rights organizations (SMI, ASCAP, etc.), ti~ings, any credits to arrangers or acconpanists, names of engineers, list of musicians with instruments played, exact recording date(s), studio location(s), album liner credits, and any information required to be submitted to unions, if applicable, guilds or other third parties."
  },
  {
    "id": "c009",
    "name": "3.05. Mechanical Licenses",
    "text": "3.05. Grantor shall secure on behalf of PRI from the copyright proprietors of compositions not subject to compulsory license, and embodied on Recordings to be delivered to PRI hereunder, executed mechanical licenses on the terms provided in Article 9 of this agreement granting PRI the right to make and distribute Phonograph Records embodying such Recordings."
  },
  {
    "id": "c010",
    "name": "3.06. Recording Content Restrictions",
    "text": "3.06. Artist's performances hereunder shall be reasonably consistent in concept an1 style and Master Recordings delivered hereunder will be similar in general artistic concept and style to Master Recordings previously delivered hereunder. Grantor further agrees that neither -live- performances nor multiple LP Albums, or jOint recordings with other royalty-receiving artists, or recordings which were not made in compliance with the material provisions of this agreement shall be recorded as part of the Minimum Recording Obligation without PRI' s prior writtfln consent, and that with respect to each Album of the Minimum Recording Obligation hereunder, Grantor shall not deliver more than three (3) Master Recordings consisting solely of instrumental recordings without PRI's prior written consent, provided: however, that if any Album of the Minimum Recording Obligation is comprised of ten (10) or more Sides, Grantor shall have the right to deliver four (4) Master Recordings consisting solely of instrumental recordings with respect to such Album. Without limitation of the generality of the foregoing, any multiple LP Album delivered hereunder shall be deemed a single LP for the purposes of product delivery and payment therefor. PRI agrees that it shall not require Grantor to record any multiple LP Album hereunder or to record with other royalty-receiving artists."
  },
  {
    "id": "c011",
    "name": "4.01(a). First Album Delivery",
    "text": "4. DELIVERY PROCEDURE 4.01. (a) The first Album of the Minimum Recording Obligation in the Initial Period and the first Album of the Minimum Recording Obligation in each of the Option Periods, if any, shall be delivered no later than one hundred twenty (120) days following conrnencement of such Period."
  },
  {
    "id": "c012",
    "name": "4.01(b). Second Album Delivery",
    "text": "(b) The second Album comprising the remainder of the Minimum Recording Obligation in the Initial Period and the second Album comprising the remainder of the Minimum Recording Obligation in each of the Option Periods, 1f any, shall be delivered no earlier than six (6) months and no later than ten (10) months following delivery of the first Album in the applicable Contract Period."
  },
  {
    "id": "c013",
    "name": "4.01(c). Extension of Delivery Dates",
    "text": "(c) ~otwithstanding the foregoing, it is understood and agreed that if PRI and Grantor mutually agree in writing, based on good business judgment and based on Artist's then-existing tour commitments, the above-stated delivery dates may be reasonably extended, provided, however, that no delivery date shall be extended for more than two (2) months after the applicable delivery date provided for in para~'raph 4. 01(a) or 4.0l(b)."
  },
  {
    "id": "c014",
    "name": "4.01(d)(i). Delivery Grace Period",
    "text": "(d) Notwithstanding anything to the contrary expressed or implied in this paragraph 4.01, it is expressly understood and agreed that (i) Grantor shall not be deemed to have failed to comply with the delivery obligations set forth in this paragraph 4.01 and/or otherwise breached this agreement if it delivers the Master Recordings hereunder within sixty (60) days follo¥ling the applicable delivery date{s) set forth in paragraphs 4.01(a) or 4.01(b), as the same may be extended pursuant to paragraph 4.01(c):"
  },
  {
    "id": "c015",
    "name": "4.01(d)(ii). Co-Producer Delay",
    "text": "at) if thg parties cannot mutually agree Oft the selection of the other co-producer referred to in paragraph 3.02(i) above, then the delivery date of the Album concerned shall be suspended until such time as the parties so agree."
  },
  {
    "id": "c016",
    "name": "4.02. Conditions of Delivery and Waiver",
    "text": "4.02. Satisfactory completion by Grantor of the procedures in Article 3 and this Article 4 shall be the necessary condition to determine whether any Recording has been delivered within the meaning of this agreement. PRI's election to nake a payment ~hich was to have been made upon delivery of Recordings or release such Recording shall not be deemed to be its acknowledgment that such delivery was properly made, and PRZ shall not be deemed to have waived either its right to require such complete and proper performance thereafte~ or its remedies for Grantor's failure to perform in accordance herewith, but any Master Recording delivered by Grantor hereunder, accepted by PRr toward fulfillment of the applicable Minimum RecQrding Obligation, and released by PRI on Records hereunder shall count in satisfaction of the Minimum Recording Obligation."
  },
  {
    "id": "c017",
    "name": "4.03. Recording Recency and Sequencing",
    "text": "4.03. Unless Grantor and PRI'~ Senior Vice President, BUsiness Affairs, mutually agree otherwise in writing, all Master Recordings delivered hereunder shall be recorded no earlier than six (6) months prior to delivery to PRI and shall ~ot embody Co~positions which have been previously recorded by Artist (whether as a group or an individual). Grantor shall not commence recording any Album (other than the first Album) prior to ninety (90) days after delivery to PR! of Master Recordings constituting the immediately preceding Album."
  },
  {
    "id": "c018",
    "name": "4.04(a). PRI Delivery-Date Notice",
    "text": "4.04. (al PRI shall send Grantor written notice of the date which PRI deems to be the applicable delivery date of Master Recordings hereunder. I f Grantor disputes the date of such notice, Grantor shall give notice in writing to PRE within thirty (30) days of PRI's notice to Grantor. Grantor's failure to so notify PRI shall be deemed Grantor· s acceptance of the date contained in PRI's notice."
  },
  {
    "id": "c019",
    "name": "4.04(b). Grantor Delivery-Date Notice",
    "text": "(b) If Grantor has not received any notice from PRl pursl:.ant to paragraph 4.04 (a) above as to the applicable delivety date within thirty (30) days after the date Grantor deems to be such applicable delivery date, then Grantor shall notify PRI within fifteen (15) days after such thirty (30) day period of the date Grantor deems the applicable d~livery date. PRI shall have the right to object to such date within thirty ~30) days after r&ceipt of Grantor's notice."
  },
  {
    "id": "c020",
    "name": "4.04(c). Disputed or Deemed Delivery Date",
    "text": "(c) If either party objects to the aate contained in the notice given by the other party, PRI and Grantor shall mutually and in good faith agree in writing on the date to be deemed the delivery date. If the parties do not reach such agreement or if neither party gives notice of the delivery date of Master Recordings as provided above earlier than thirty (30) days prior to the date of initial release in the United States of such Master Recordings, then the delivery date of such Album shall be deemed to be thirty (30) days prior to such date of initial release."
  },
  {
    "id": "c021",
    "name": "5.01(a). Ownership and Exploitation Rights",
    "text": "5. RIGHTS 5.01. (a) Each Master Recording recorded hereunder shall be considered a ·work made for hire·. All Master Recordings delivered hereunder or recorded by Artist during the Term and the performances contained thereon and Recordings deriv~d therefrom shall from inception of their creation be entirely the property of PRI in perpetuity throughout the world, under copyright and otherwise, free of any claim whatsoever by Grantor or by Artist or any other Persons, and PRI shall have the right to register the copyrights in such Master Recordings and Recordings derived therefrom in PRI's name or in the name(s) of PRIes designee(s} and to secure any and all r~newals and extensions thereof. Without limiting the generality of the foregOing, Artist and Grantor hereby assign to PRI all of Artist's and Grantor's right and title to the copyright:> in perpetuity throughout the world in and to such Master Recordings, Recordings derived therefrom and any and all renewals and extensions of such copyrights, and PRI and its 0714/50S0A/0784A/5271A P85-1S6 CONFIDENTIAL UMG-MAL 001343 - 7 - subsidiaries, affiliates, and licensees shall have the sole, exclusive and unlimited right throughout the world to manufacture Records, by any methode s} now or hereafter known embodying any portiones) or all of the performances embodied on Master Recordings hereunder; to publicly p~rform such Records; to import, export, sell, transfer, lease, rent, deal in or otherwise dispose of such Master Recordings and Records derived therefrom throughout the world under any trademarks, trade names or labels designated by PRI: to edit or adapt the Haster Recordings hereunder to conform to the technological or commercial requirements of Phonograph Records in various formats now or hereafter known or developed, or to eliminate material which, in the reasonable opinion o~ PRI's counsel, would subject PRI to any civil or criminal action: to use the Master Recordings hereunder for background music, synchronization in motion pictures and television soundtracks and other similar purposes, including, without limitation, use on transportation facilities; notwithstanding the provisions of this agreement, except the provisions of paragraphs 5.01(c) and S.OI(d) hereof, PRI and its subsidiaries, affiliates' and licensees may, at their election, delay or refrain from doing anyone or more of the foregoing."
  },
  {
    "id": "c022",
    "name": "5.01(b)(i). Out-Takes",
    "text": "(b) Notwithstanding anything to the contrary contained in paragraph 5.01(a) above, ~ith respect to sales of Records in the United States during the Term: (i) PRI will not utilize for Phonograph Record purposes out-takes of any Master Recording delivered to PRI hereunder without Grantor's prior written consent."
  },
  {
    "id": "c023",
    "name": "5.01(b)(ii). Coupling Restrictions",
    "text": "(ii) Except with respect to promotional Records, Audia-Visual Recordings or Records used in connection with public transporatation carriers for facilities, PRI will not, in the United States, during anyone (1) calendar year of the Term, couple more than two (2} Master Recordings delivered he::eunder with Master Recordings not embodying Artist's performances without Grantor's consent, which shall not be unreasonably withheld;"
  },
  {
    "id": "c024",
    "name": "5.01(b)(iii). Initial Release Label",
    "text": "(iii) 'i:'he initial release in the United States during the Term of each Album of the Minimu~ Recording Obligation hereunder shall be on a label used by PRI at the time of such release for RecQrdings of PRI's top ·pop· artists then under exclusive term contract to PRI."
  },
  {
    "id": "c025",
    "name": "5.01(b)(iv). Budget Records",
    "text": "(iv) PRI will not, without Grantor's prior written consent which shall not be unreasonably withheld, release as a Budget Record in the United States during the Term any Album delivered hereunder as part of the Minimum Recording Obligation until twenty-four (24) months after the initial United States release of such Album."
  },
  {
    "id": "c026",
    "name": "5.01(b)(v). Mid-Price Records",
    "text": "(v) PRI will not, without Grantor's prior written consent, Which shall not be unreasonably withheld, release as a Mid-Price Record any Album delivered hereunder as part of the Minimum Recording Obligation until eighteen (18) months after the initial United States release of such Album."
  },
  {
    "id": "c027",
    "name": "5.01(b)(vi). Premium Use",
    "text": "(vi) PRI shall not license the Master .Recordings hereunder for premium use wi thout Grantor's prior consent."
  },
  {
    "id": "c028",
    "name": "5.01(b)(vii)(A). Album Artwork",
    "text": "(vii) (A) In connection with the initial release in the United States of each Album, PRI shall consult with Grantor regarding the preparation of artwork for the Album cover (-Artwork-) and Grantor shall have the right to approve such Artwork, provided that such approval shall not be unreasonably withheld. PRI shall be responsible for arranging appointments with Grantor, at a mutually convenient time, sufficiently far in advance of the scheduled release date of the applicable Album to allow Grantor to timely eXercise the above right of consultation and approval. Grantor's approval shall be deemed given within five (5) days following Grantor's receipt of PRI's written request therefor unless Grantor notifies PRI of its specific objections within such five (5) day period. After Grantor's exercise of such right of consultation and approval, PRI shall have the right to prepare and use such Artwork in accordance with the communications between Grantor and PRI during Grantor's exercise: if Grantor fails to exercise such right, PRI shall have the right to prepare and use such Artwork without any further right of consultation or approval by Grantor. All rights in and to any Artwork or related material furnished by Grantor or at Grantor's request, including the copyright and renewals and extensions thereof, shall be PRI's property throughout the world in perpetuity. All matters relating to trademarks, notices, including, without limitation, upe symbols (i.e., bar-coding), or disclosures reasonably deemed advisable by PRI's attorneys, and any matter other than the Album cover layout and the picture or art to be used on the cover, will be determined in PRr f s sole discretion, provided, however, that PRI expressly agrees that unless required by law, PRI shall not af fix any sticker or other deSignation pertaining to explici t lyrics on the packages of Records hereunder without Grantor's prior consent."
  },
  {
    "id": "c029",
    "name": "5.01(b)(vii)(B). Foreign Artwork",
    "text": "(B) With respect to sales of Albums outside the United States, PRI will request its licensees outside the United states to utilize the same Artwork as is utilized by PRI in connection with the initial United States release of the applicable Album; if Grantor notifies PRI of sales of Albums outside the United States in violation of the prOVisions of this paragraph 5.0l(b)(vii)(B), PRI will instruct its licensees to discontinue such violative sales, but neither PRI nor its licensees shall have any liability by reason of such sales occurring prior to PRIIs receipt nf such notice, and PRI shall have no liability by reason of such sales at any time."
  },
  {
    "id": "c030",
    "name": "5.01(b)(viii). Editing Masters",
    "text": "(viii) PRI shall not, in connection with the initial United States release of Records embodying Master Recordings hereunder, edit the Master Recordings hereunder except as necessary for the release of Singles, or non-disc configurations, or to eliminate material which. in the opinion of PRlis counsel, would constitute a defamation, libel or violate or infringe upon any right, including, without limitation, the right of privacy, of any Person; provided, hO\\leVer, that the parties shall mutually agree, based on good business judgment and reasonableness, whether any such editing is necessary and that PRI shall offer to Grantor the first o~portunity to so edit the Master Recordings (unless same would interfere with a scheduled release date), which editing ~hal1 be completed with Artist present Within seven (7) business days following PRI' s notice to Grantor, and which offer shall be deemed rejected i f Grantor does not respond and/or complete such editing within said seven (7) business day period. It is understood and agreed that the costs of any such editing shall be at. PRI' s expense, shall not be deemed attributable to the applicable Recording Fund provided for in paragraph 6.01 belowJ but shall constitute an Advance hereunder."
  },
  {
    "id": "c031",
    "name": "5.01(b)(ix)(A). Greatest Hits Limit",
    "text": "(ix) (A) PRI will not, in the United States, without Grantor's consent, not to be unreasonably withheld, release during the Term more than three (3) Albums in the form of a ·Greatest Hits· compilation consisting entirely of Master Recordings recorded hereunder."
  },
  {
    "id": "c032",
    "name": "5.01(b)(ix)(B). Greatest Hits Selection",
    "text": "(B) If PRI elects to release one (l) or more ·Greatest Hits· Albums in the United States, then PRI shall submit to Grantor a written proposal of the Master Recordings recorded hereunder to be included on such -Greatest Hits· Album, and Grantor shall have the right to object to any or all of the Master Recordings proposed by PRI and to recommend alternative MAster Recordings to be included within 0774/5JdOA/0784A/5271A P85-1S6 -------_....... _---_.,,---- ......-. EM p • CONFIDENTIAL UMG-MAL 001346 - 10 - five (5) business days after Grantorls receipt of PRIls proposal. In no event shall Grantor have the right to object to any Master Recording embodied in a Single which achieved a position in the -Top 100· chart of any national trade publication at any time prior to the initial release of such Greatest Hits Album. . If Grantor does so object to the inclusion in any such -Greatest Hits- Album of any Master Recordings proposed by PRI, each of PRI and Grantor ~hall select one-half (1/2) of the Master Recordings so disputed, provided that if the number of disputed Master Recordings is an odd number, PRI shall have the right to select one more Master Recording than Grantor. If Grantor does not object to c:ny of the Master Recordings proposed by PRI, or does not respond within said five (5) day period, the Master Recordings proposed by PRI shall be included on such ·Greatest Hits· Album. The advance payable for each such -Greatest Hits· Album shall be as provided in paragraph 6.0l(d) below."
  },
  {
    "id": "c033",
    "name": "5.01(b)(x). Compact Disc Release",
    "text": "(K) If commercially possible, PRI shall release each Album of the Minimum Recording Obligation hereunder on a compact disc configuration within one hundred twenty (120) days following the initial United States release of such Album in the Minimum Recording Obligation."
  },
  {
    "id": "c034",
    "name": "5.01(b)(xi). Condition on Limitations",
    "text": "(xi) The provisions of paragraph 5.01(b) above shall not apply if Grantor has not Materially fulfilled its delivery obligations described in Articles 3 and 4 above with respect to any Master Recordings hereunder within the time periods set forth in such Articles, subject to the tetms of paragraph 4.01Cd) above."
  },
  {
    "id": "c035",
    "name": "5.01(c). Failure to Release in United States",
    "text": "(e) Provided that Grantor has fulfilled all of its material obligations hereunder, and the Master Recordings for each Album of t.he Minimum Recording Obligation hereunder are delivered within the time periods set forth in Article 4 above, subject to the terms of paragraph 4.0lCd) above, if PRI does not release each Album of the Minimum Recording Obligation in the United States on or before sixty (60) days following the date of delivery to PRI of such Album, then Grantor may, within thirty (30) days following the expiration of such sixty (60) day period, give PRI notice of such failure so to release such Album. PRI shall eit.her cure such failure within sixty (60) days after PRI's receipt of such notice, or Grantor shall have the right by wri tten notice to PHI '.... i thin thirty (30) days following the expiration of such sixty (60) day period to terminate the Term of this agreement. If Grantor shall exercise such right of termination, Grantor shall have the 0774/5080A/0784A/527lA P85-1S6 ~--~-----' ---~------------------------------~---------- ............ CONFIDENTIAL UMG-MAL 001347 - 11 - right to require that all rights in the unreleased Album be assigned to Grantor by notice to PRI and repayment to PRI of all monies paid by PRI in connection therewith, payable within thirty (30) days after expiration of such sixty (60) day period, and, in the event the unreleased Album is the first Album of the Minimum Recording Obligation in any Contract Per iod, to require that P1U pay to Grantor, and within thirty (30) days following PRIes receipt of Grantor's notice PRI shall pay to Grantor, the Advance otherwise payable with respect to the second Album of the Minimum Recording Obligation in such Contract Period as set forth in paragraph 6.01(b) below. In addition, Grantor shall payor cause to be paid to PRl a royalty of two percent (2') of the Royalty Base for Net Sales in the United States of the unreleased Album, with proportionate reductions on all sales of Records embodying the Master Recordings constituting such unreleased Album for which reduced royalties are payable under this agreement, ~nd Grantor shall, or shall cause any Person who distributes such Records to, account to PRl pursuant to the terms and conditions of Article 8 below, and PRl shall have the same right to audit Grantor as is set forth in Article B below, and/or the right to audit such third party distributor in the same manner as Grantor may audit such third party distributor. If Grantor exercises its right of termination with respect to such unreleased Album in accordance with this paragraph, Grantor' s said right shall be subject to the following terms and conditions:"
  },
  {
    "id": "c036",
    "name": "5.01(c)(i). Consents and Third-Party Obligations",
    "text": "C i) Grantor will be required to obtain and deliver to PRl all consents required by PRI, including the consent of Artist, and all agreements which PRl may require for any third party to look to Grantor, and not to PRr, for the fulfillment of any obligations arising in connection with the manufacture or distribution of Records derived from such unreleased Master Recordings (including such agreements by unions and funds established under union agreements). Grantor will also become a first party to the Phonograph Record Manufacturers' Special Payments Fund Agreement with the American Federation of Musicians, or any successor agreement then in effect, if applicable. The provisions of paragraph S.Ollc} with respect to the unreleased Master Recordings will not become effective until Grantor has complied with all the provisions of this subeection 5.01(c)(i)."
  },
  {
    "id": "c037",
    "name": "5.01(c)(ii). Payments and Legal Compliance",
    "text": "(it) Grantor will make all payments required in connection with the manufacture, sale or distribution of Records made from those unreleased Master Recordings after the effective date of the termination, including, withont limitation, all royalties and other payments to performing artists, producers, owners of copyrights in mUsical 0774/50BOA/0184A/5271A P85-IS6 , ':\"- .. ... .p''''' ,\" • CONFIDENTIAL UMG-MAL 001348 • ... - 12 - compositions, the Music Performance Trust rund and Special Payments Fund, and any other unions and union funds. Grantor will comply with the applicable rules and regulations of the American Federation of Musicians and any other applicable laws, rules and regulations covering any use of the Master Recordings by Grantor."
  },
  {
    "id": "c038",
    "name": "5.01(c)(iii). Warranty Disclaimer and Indemnity",
    "text": "(iii) No warranty or representation, express or implied, will be made by PRI in connection with the applicable Master Recordings or otherwise r except war ranties relating to PRI's ownership rights as provided in ~ara9raph 5.01(a) above. Grantor will indemnify and hold harmless PRI and its licensees against all claims, damages, liabilities, costs, and expenses, including reasonable counsel fees, arising out of any use of the unreleased Master Recordings or exercise of such rights by Grantor."
  },
  {
    "id": "c039",
    "name": "5.01(c). Suspension of Notice Periods",
    "text": "The running of each of the aforementioned thirty (30) and ~ixty (60) day periods will be suspended for the period of any suspensiQn of the Term of this agreement. For purposes of computing said periods, the months of November and December shall not be counted."
  },
