  {"clause_id": "c013", "issues": [
    {"issue": "Delivery dates \"may be reasonably extended\" if the parties \"mutually agree in writing, based on good business judgment\" — an agreement-to-agree qualified by two undefined standards. Whether either party could refuse an extension is unresolved.", "type": 1, "prob": 0.23},
    {"issue": null, "type": 2, "prob": 0.09}
  ]},
  {"clause_id": "c014", "issues": [
    {"issue": null, "type": 1, "prob": 0.12},
    {"issue": "Paragraph 4.01(d)(i) says late delivery within sixty days is not a failure to comply or a breach, but paragraph 6.01(c) reduces the Advance by 10% per month from \"the last date such Album would otherwise be timely delivered pursuant to paragraph 4.01\". Whether the sixty-day grace shifts that Final Date cannot be resolved from the two provisions read together.", "type": 2, "prob": 0.31}
  ]},
  {"clause_id": "c015", "issues": [
    {"issue": "Saying the \"delivery date ... shall be suspended until such time as the parties so agree\" is imprecise — a date cannot be suspended, and the clause gives no outer limit or mechanism if the parties never agree on the co-producer. The effect on the Contract Period and the Term is left open.", "type": 1, "prob": 0.28},
    {"issue": null, "type": 2, "prob": 0.13}
